    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Green Sun's Zenith for X=0 could search for Dryad Arbor (a common inclusion in Modern GSZ decks) to ramp, or at minimum shuffles itself back into the library for future use. However, even without Dryad Arbor in the deck, GSZ for X=0 fetches any green creature with mana value 0. Young Wolf is a key piece for the Agatha's Soul Cauldron combo (providing undying), so playing it directly is defensible. That said, if the deck runs Dryad Arbor, GSZ for X=0 would have been strictly better here as it ramps while preserving Young Wolf in hand for a later combo turn with Cauldron. The reasoning explicitly dismissed GSZ for X=0 without considering what it could find, suggesting a missed opportunity.",
